# Modules the initramfs needs, in dependency order.
#
# Almost none, and this file exists to say that deliberately.
# modules-initfs.downstream is a
# hundred lines long because the stock 5.10 tree builds its whole SoC support
# as loadable modules and the initramfs has to name every one in probe order.
# Our mainline config does the opposite: the clock controller, pinctrl, the
# SPMI arbiter, the RPMh regulators, the SMMU, sdhci-msm, the GENI serial
# console, dwc3 and the HS PHY are all CONFIG_*=y, so they are in vmlinux and
# have probed before the initramfs runs at all.
#
# The USB gadget functions are modules (CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS=m), but
# postmarketos-initramfs already lists usb_f_acm, usb_f_ncm, usb_f_rndis and
# usb_f_mass_storage in its own 00-default.modules, and mkinitfs follows
# modinfo dependencies from there, so libcomposite, u_ether and u_serial come
# along without being named. ext4 and the crypto it needs are on that list
# too.
#
# If something here ever stops being builtin, it belongs in this file rather
# than in the config.
#
# There are two exceptions.
#
# The touchscreen, whose driver the config builds as a module. Without it
# here the initramfs' on-screen keyboard, buffyboard in the debug shell or
# unl0kr for an encrypted rootfs, has no touch input. Touch through it was
# verified at the phone on 2026-10-11.
#
# The graphics clock controller, which provides the GDSCs the GPU and its
# SMMU sit in. drm/msm is built in, so the GPU probes early and defers until
# this module appears - but only until the driver core's deferred-probe
# timeout, ten seconds after late_initcall. After that genpd answers
# -ETIMEDOUT instead of -EPROBE_DEFER, the SMMU's and the GPU's probes fail
# for good, and loading the module later binds only the clock controller.
# Round 71 hit exactly that; status doc, rounds 71 and 72. From the
# initramfs it loads within a few seconds of boot.
edt-ft5x06
gpucc-sm6450
